    "summary": "The pager gains prepend(page): a page for the shown session that ends at the first held index is rendered through the registry with its pending rows isolated and following off, moved above the held rows, and the scroll position moved by the height added; any other page is discarded. requestOlder posts one load-older at a time, cleared by the matching page, a reset or a 5 second wait. A scroll listener asks for a page at the top and trims on return to the bottom. The 'load earlier' bar shows the count of older rows while any exist. A row that cannot be rendered falls back to a plain line.",
